      c4: { line: "She is a long time finding the words. \"Two.\" Then, entirely level: \"I burnt the first one. I wrote two and I burnt the first one in this grate on the tenth of September and I have been standing in a shut house for eleven years with the other one on the table deciding whether to be brave.\" She looks at the door. \"I asked you to bring me the name. I did not tell you the name was going to walk in on its own.\"" },
      c6: { line: "\"A gent. with a copper plate on his shoe.\" Her hand goes to the table and holds it. \"Frank had a pair of shoes with copper on them because he was in the docks and you went about a yard in them, and he lost them in the river in 1938, and I never once thought about the river, because he was alive and the river was where my sister was.\" She is not crying; she has gone somewhere past it. \"He stood in a doorway on the eleventh of September and asked a lockkeeper how deep it was.\"" },
      c17: { line: "\"You have not asked me about the coat once.\" She almost laughs. \"That is why you are the first man in eleven years I have told. I have had two policemen and a newspaper man and a man from the church, and every one of them began with the coat, and I have watched the coat take eleven years off the life of my sister, and the coat is a coat, and I bought it.\"" }
