      c7: { line: "\"No boots.\" He is the first man in this case to react to anything. \"No boots, and I have not said one word about that in eleven years because I have been a good husband to a woman who killed her sister and I did not think that was a thing you were allowed to say out loud in a house.\" He puts a hand on the gate. \"I want to say it out loud. I have wanted to say it out loud every day for eleven years.\"" },
      c11: { line: "\"A foreign scarf, and a pair of size nines that were never produced.\" He is quite still. \"My scarf was Egyptian. I bought it in Alexandria in 1934 because a man in a docker's cap in a photograph ought to have something. I gave it away in the September of 1937 because I had come to believe my wife was going to be all right, and I have not thought about it since, and I have just thought about it, and I am going to have to sit down in a gateway.\"" }
